u  create we won't any language we put down  will be crystal clear and unequivocal on  that point now not only have I been  talking to tons of d d players and GMS  I've also been talking to Wizards of the  Coast lawyers now there's tons of stuff  going on behind the scenes but all the  lawyers will officially say is that  their statement is sincere typical  lawyers just the worst but look it's  great that they listen to the criticism  I'm sure that the changes will mollify a  lot of what people are currently upset  about but I think the point remains if  you're only making content that is DND  compatible and doesn't reproduce their  IP well maybe you never needed to comply  with the ogl in the first place maybe  the real ogl was the friends that we  made along the way smoke bomb  now normally I would not cover a topic  like this this is way too nerdy even for  me and it's way too in the weeds uh  normally a subject like this would be  covered by a fellow YouTube Attorney  Richard Hogue a few days after Christmas  he suffered a stroke was rushed to the  hospital and underwent extensive brain  surgery it seems like he's through the  worst of it but regardless he's going to  have an extensive recovery period and  Richard has always been a straight  shooter and his YouTube channel Hogue  law has always been a resource for  insightful legal commentary on a lot of  legal minutia and his channel as many of  you know is focused on the gaming and  video game industry things that Richard  is incredibly passionate about this is  exactly the kind of video that he would  have loved to have made if he'd been  able to  um his road to recovery is going to be  long his sister has created a GoFundMe  page called reasonable Minds can rebuild  because one of Richard's famous phrases  is that reasonable Minds can differ  because he wasn't afraid to offer an  unpop popular opinion because reasonable  Minds can differ especially when it  comes to the law and that's always been  an incredi